3be7de\", \"bytes\": 49109, \"media_type\": \"text/xml\"}}, {\"id\": \"jpal-indonesia\", \"title\": \"J-PAL: doubling teacher salaries in Indonesia\", \"url\": \"https://www.povertyactionlab.org/evaluation/impact-doubling-teacher-salary-student-performance-indonesia?lang=en\", \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-07T10:38:11.594824Z\", \"artifact\": {\"sha256\": \"1cdc67d26467180e851dfd3d90fd36eb8ff0d8cb8a1b21aa666d9a2b54d191d5\", \"bytes\": 101519, \"media_type\": \"text/html\"}}, {\"id\": \"hendricks-texas\", \"title\": \"Hendricks: teacher salaries and retention in Texas\", \"url\": \"https://files.eric.ed.gov/fulltext/ED627846.pdf\", \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-07T10:38:11.119693Z\", \"artifact\": {\"sha256\": \"4855a74984afc0dac9897fc3b5b7d78183696cca9b29474cb3de784f5caf9dcb\", \"bytes\": 566170, \"media_type\": \"application/pdf\"}}], \"shared_evidence\": [{\"claim\": \"The exact population is National NT, all students including public and nonpublic schools; mathematics MRPCM composite, grade 8, TOTAL, MN:MN, R3 accommodations permitted. NP is a different public-only population.\", \"source_ids\": [\"naep-api\", \"naep-population\"]}, {\"claim\": \"The shared history contains current official API unrounded means. The target is the publisher whole-number mean; 2019, 2022 and 2024 published NT anchors are 282, 274 and 274. These captures do not prove the historical first print. Do not substitute NP values.\", \"source_ids\": [\"naep-history\", \"naep-summary\", \"naep-reporting\"]}, {\"claim\": \"NCES estimates Winter 2030 assessment and Fall 2030 report release; there is no verified exact publication day. A framework update starts in 2026. Treat comparability, cohort recovery and irregular assessment intervals explicitly, without assuming independent annual changes.\", \"source_ids\": [\"naep-calendar\", \"naep-framework\"]}, {\"claim\": \"H.R. 2021 was introduced March 10, 2025 and referred to the House Committee on Education and Workforce. The official status XML captured September 7, 2026 contains no enacted-law record. This describes the captured state, not the future condition result.\", \"source_ids\": [\"hr2021-status\"]}, {\"claim\": \"Introduced H.R. 2021 section 3 proposes four-year state grants for a $60,000 teacher salary floor for school year 2026-27 with inflation adjustment. State applications and sustainability assurances are required; at least 85% goes to local-agency subgrants, with Title I and rural priorities. Qualifying schools are public elementary/secondary schools. Section 8 authorizes such sums as necessary for FY2026-30; it does not appropriate a fixed funding amount.\", \"source_ids\": [\"hr2021-text\"]}, {\"claim\": \"H.R. 2021 section 3(c) requires grants to supplement and not supplant other Federal, State and local public funds for teacher base salaries; prohibits reducing or adjusting teacher pay or state teacher loan forgiveness due to grant eligibility; and requires the same state/local compensation funds for each teacher and school as absent the Act. Do not treat simple replacement of planned state/local teacher compensation spending as permitted implementation. Any crowd-out rationale must distinguish prohibited noncompliance or weak enforcement from a separately explained indirect fiscal adjustment consistent with these rules.\", \"source_ids\": [\"hr2021-text\"]}, {\"claim\": \"J-PAL describes a randomized acceleration of salary doubling for eligible incumbent teachers in Indonesia: 120 treatment schools and 240 controls, 360 total. No detectable student test-score improvement after 2-3 years was reported. This is not proof of exactly zero effect, and no direct conversion to U.S. national NAEP points follows.\", \"source_ids\": [\"jpal-indonesia\"]}, {\"claim\": \"Hendricks estimates a Texas salary-turnover elasticity of -1.4. His retention-only simulation of a 5% salary increase projects average teacher value-added gains of 0.0005 SD within 3 years and 0.0007 SD within 10 years. These are modeled teacher-productivity changes, not observed national NAEP gains. Turnover includes district moves. Do not linearly scale these figures to a large nationwide salary floor or treat district recruitment gains as national net gains.\", \"source_ids\": [\"hendricks-texas\"]}], \"limitations\": [\"Exploratory local-operator forecasts; neither prospective registration nor calibrated causal policy-effect estimates.\", \"No automatic condition or numeric-outcome resolver is registered. These scenarios cannot enter ranks or training rewards.\", \"NCES estimates a Fall 2030 release but has not supplied an exact day. Historical API means are current-vintage captures, not authenticated original-release prints.\", \"Enactment can occur with amendments; the forecast assumes the introduced grant mechanism materially survives. Funding and implementation are modeled assumptions.\", \"Public-school effects need not generalize to the full NT population. Indonesia and district-level Texas evidence do not identify a national U.S. NAEP effect.\", \"The difference between marginal conditional forecast medians has no identified causal interpretation or uncertainty interval without a joint model.\"], \"methodology\": \"paired_conditional_v1\", \"status\": \"exploratory\", \"scoring_status\": \"not_registered\", \"trust_class\": \"local_operator\"}, \"response_schema\": {\"$defs\": {\"CdfPoint\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"value\": {\"title\": \"Value\", \"type\": \"number\"}, \"probability\": {\"title\": \"Probability\", \"type\": \"number\"}}, \"required\": [\"value\", \"probability\"], \"title\": \"CdfPoint\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CdfSummary\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"pointEstimate\": {\"title\": \"Pointestimate\", \"type\": \"number\"}, \"median\": {\"title\": \"Median\", \"type\": \"number\"}, \"interval80\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CdfSupport\"}}, \"required\": [\"pointEstimate\", \"median\", \"interval80\"], \"title\": \"CdfSum